# Fixed defect 131's second round, 2026-09-29, a declaration head whose line
# goes on past it. Symptom: `test "t" )`, `record Point )` and
# `variant Token )` over their bodies were named as a missing body, an empty
# record and an empty variant, once each, and the body, the fields and the
# cases below were dropped whole with every mistake inside them. Cause: the
# recovery after the report, `cursor.recover_to_next_decl`, drops the block
# under the line. The rest of the line is dropped and what is below read, as
# after a statement head whose line goes on; the message is the one it was.
#
# Moved 2026-09-29 by defect 133's lane, given defect 131's class from this
# case's own lane: over fields and cases that are there, `empty_record` and
# `empty_variant` named them missing, so the record's and the variant's
# report is now the head's junk, `expected_end_of_line`, with where the
# members go. The `test` line keeps `missing_body` (found `)`): its message
# is `parse/opening.hero`'s, which that lane's repair did not reach.

test "a name and more" )  #~ missing_body
    y = 3 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

record Point )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    x: )  #~ expected_type

variant Token )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    a
    )  #~ expected_case

function main()
    print(1)
